1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,200
How does AI find the best weights out of

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:02,672
billions?

3
00:00:02,987 --> 00:00:04,665
It slides down a loss landscape.

4
00:00:05,117 --> 00:00:07,450
At any point, the tangent slope gives the

5
00:00:07,450 --> 00:00:07,927
gradient.

6
00:00:08,245 --> 00:00:10,525
It points steepest uphill, so we step in

7
00:00:10,525 --> 00:00:10,949
reverse.

8
00:00:11,379 --> 00:00:13,452
Scaled by the learning rate eta, each

9
00:00:13,452 --> 00:00:15,628
gradient step descends toward the minimum.

10
00:00:17,838 --> 00:00:20,099
Where the curve flattens, the gradient

11
00:00:20,099 --> 00:00:21,037
vanishes to zero.

12
00:00:21,368 --> 00:00:23,464
The descent converges, locking into

13
00:00:23,464 --> 00:00:24,347
optimal weights.

